 "finding": "The macOS arm64 drift is entirely the Metal GPU backend. With CRISPEMBED_FORCE_CPU=1, the same macOS package matches Linux arm64 within 5.14e-7 and Linux x86_64 at 1.20e-4/0.9999996977 (strict pass) on macos-14 and macos-15. With default selection, it reproduces the stored v4 macOS vector within 5e-7. CPU compile differences (AppleClang, Accelerate, llamafile, -march, fp-contract) contribute at most 5.14e-7.",
 "source_level_cause": "Not op-replayed: backend selection, not CPU code, causes the drift. Unverified hypothesis: Metal IQ4_XS mul_mv keeps F32 activations, while the CPU path quantizes activations to Q8_K.",
 "build_fix": "None applies: no CPU build-config alignment changes the vector by more than 5.14e-7. Release builds are unchanged.",
 "limits": [
  "Hosted paravirtual Metal device only; physical Apple GPUs may use different kernels (simdgroup paths).",
  "Single model and fixture text.",
